Z||000000||Adrift||06-29-2001||04:50 PM||||I went to Standard auto wreckers (http://www.standardautowreckers.com) today. First time I've ever been to a junk yard - pretty neat. Well, I went looking for a restorable fiero, but didn't find any. There were two fieros there though, both stacked on top of other cars. I thought some people in this forum might be interested in them so I took pictures and am posting them below. Sorry I couldn't get into the engine bay, as I said the cars were about 6 feet off the ground and I didn't feel safe climbing into them.<P>One of the cars is Automatic, the other is stick.<P>I know these aren't that useful but I hope this helps someone out there! Maybe save one of you a trip?<P>Ari (Adrift)<P>------------------<BR>My Dream Fiero, you ask?<BR>That would be a automatic '86 or newer V6 GT Fastback with T-Tops and A/C, fully running and for sale for under $1000 CAN. Know someone who's selling a car like this for this price in the Toronto area? PLEASE E-MAIL ME!!!<p>[This message has been edited by Adrift (edited 06-30-2001).]||||reg||1
