Z||000005||fierohoho||06-29-2001||06:04 PM||||I think you would be better off getting a Fiero in running order, think about it, if you need parts you found a junk yard with only 2 cars. If you find something elsewhere and have to travel or pay shipping it adds up fast. Those cars looked pretty picked over too. Best bet I've seen is to check the back row in the weeds at used car dealers, the small time outfits, I've seen some pretty good deals in that situation as they are usually eager to unload them. Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
